## Remaining

- Remove redundant code. No line budget: the goal is that no logic is written twice and
  nothing unused is left behind. The rebuild was meant to do this and did not (src/ grew
  from 8,760 lines before it to 12,164 now, with no simplification goal ever set).
  Steps:
  1. Read only audit of src/ first. List every duplicated or dead piece with file:line
     evidence, each one checked by a second agent trying to prove it is NOT redundant.
     Show the list to the user before changing anything; the user picks what goes.
  2. Remove one piece at a time, each its own commit, with npm test, npm run bench,
     bench:cost and node todo-run/f46/ab.mjs unchanged before and after, plus a desktop
     and phone check. Behaviour must not change.
  Suspected (not yet audited):
  - SongRow.js and SongCardMobile.js repeat the same row logic; PlayerSections.js
    BeatmapRow may be a third copy.
  - page.js (1,545 lines) may hold per side copies of selection and download handling.
  - the same inline style objects (buttons, badges, cards) rewritten across components.
  - leftover helpers, props and exports nothing uses any more.

